{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349523,"nonce":"FhqcNQ290NdnHfitqzUi2YgLWRI=","title":"AOT executables cannot link ZRTL plugins: objects name `$Plugin$fn`, the archives define the Rust function","message":"A lowered call into a plugin is an extern named by its ZRTL symbol (`$IO$println_dynamic`, `$Tensor$add`). The JIT tiers bind those names through the plugin's runtime table (`_zrtl_symbols` after dlopen, or `static_plugin()` when linked into the host), and the LLVM JIT tier through the trampoline stubs in crates/compiler/src/llvm_link.rs. An AOT build has only the system linker, and a plugin's static archive defines the `#[no_mangle]` Rust name: `nm libzrtl_io.a` lists `io_println_dynamic`, `io_print_dynamic` and no `$IO$` symbol. The pairing of the two names exists only in the symbol table the zrtl_plugin! macro builds for run time, so nothing defines `$IO$println_dynamic` at link time.\n\nReproducer: crates/zynml/examples/test_11_fstring_number.zynml gets through `zyntax compile` (its f-string desugars straight to the `$IO$` externs), and `zyntax compile --backend llvm -g crates/zynml/ml.zyn -s crates/zynml/examples/test_11_fstring_number.zynml -o t11 --lib \u003cplugins target\u003e/release/libzrtl_io.a` fails with undefined reference to `$IO$print_dynamic` and `$IO$println_dynamic` (NUC x86_64 and Mac arm64). A program that declares the Rust names instead (`extern def io_println_i64(x: i64)`) links against the same archive and prints correctly.\n\nTwo more gaps between an AOT build and ZynML's stdlib plugins:\n- zrtl_text, zrtl_vector, zrtl_model, zrtl_tensor, zrtl_simd and zrtl_audio build no staticlib (crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]), so plugins/build_static.sh falls back to copying an .rlib, which cc cannot link.\n- Two plugin staticlibs built with default features do not link together: libzrtl_io.a with libzrtl_time.a fails with multiple definition of `_zrtl_info`, `_zrtl_symbols`, `_zrtl_set_allocator` and `_zrtl_set_immortal_table` (NUC x86_64, GNU ld). Built with `linked-into-host` the same pair links and runs. build_static.sh does not set that feature, and the book's `--lib runtime` workflow does not mention it.\n\nFix direction: at AOT link time define each referenced `$Plugin$fn` against the function the plugin table pairs it with (a generated alias or jump stub object, or have the plugin macro export the ZRTL name as a second symbol), and ship the stdlib plugins as staticlibs built with linked-into-host.","files":null}]}